<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Germany</title><subtitle type="html">Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Germany</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-ger</id><updated>2026-09-24T20:03:55Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-ger" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/s-1432?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-ger" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Extremist parties are thriving ― and that scares people</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a8d7ebd2008dd2eacf046e56634354ff0430baee294628c3e3ff4e5f3e549405</id><updated>2026-09-24T20:03:55Z</updated><published>2026-09-24T14:00:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/extremist-parties-are-thriving-_-and-that-scares-people/a-79410960--03e11a3885b2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/extremist-parties-are-thriving-―-and-that-scares-people/a-79410960?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Far-right and far-left parties are celebrating success after success, leaving moderate politicians in the dust and worrying many Germans. Political psychology helps us understand what's behind growing polarization.</summary><category term="Science" /></entry><entry><title>Germany news: Berlin officially withdraws Olympics bid</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6daf9cf57f2dd6a5c2dea987ed8b4811308d0f04f40e147bfe6d37c30e665ad6</id><updated>2026-09-24T20:02:39Z</updated><published>2026-09-24T12:42:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-news-berlin-officially-withdraws-olympics-bid/live-79406294--30622a12ce08.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-news-berlin-officially-withdraws-olympics-bid/live-79406294?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Berlin's decision to withdraw its Olympic bid means that only Munich and the western Rhine/Ruhr region are left in the running as potential Olympic hosts. DW has more.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germany: Economic institutes double growth forecast for 2026</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bb4102068e4a23c9541dda1d4a9434b0ff00b23814bcbadf1980c1f21d9c9c41</id><updated>2026-09-24T20:02:39Z</updated><published>2026-09-24T08:11:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-economic-institutes-double-growth-forecast-for-2026/a-78168080--b4403b4ba952.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-economic-institutes-double-growth-forecast-for-2026/a-78168080?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Experts predict German GDP growth will double to 1.3% this year but warn of structural difficulties ahead. The picture is complicated, they say, especially because of uncertainty in the energy sector.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Berlin Airport briefly suspends flights over drone sighting</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ce01857bcad32a2284b11392f131a225ccae30c2b3f950d01053e9f41b39161d</id><updated>2026-09-24T20:02:39Z</updated><published>2026-09-23T19:43:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/berlin-airport-briefly-suspends-flights-over-drone-sighting/a-79403865--84b3e93d15cb.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/berlin-airport-briefly-suspends-flights-over-drone-sighting/a-79403865?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Airspace over the German capital was closed for about 45 minutes after a drone was spotted on the runway. Flights have resumed but are experiencing delays.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germany news: Call to scrap once-a-day gas price rises</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6f0f96dd1482b0910e68b7f59a74e95f98c7e5451b5590886c65e4a3c7dd482b</id><updated>2026-09-24T20:02:39Z</updated><published>2026-09-23T07:25:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-news-call-to-scrap-once-a-day-gas-price-rises/live-79382523--75528f1f86f0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-news-call-to-scrap-once-a-day-gas-price-rises/live-79382523?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The ADAC motoring association says a once-a-day rule on gas price changes has failed to help drivers' wallets. Entry-level jobs are becoming scarcer, making things hard for those entering the job market. DW has more.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>After several difficult years, economists now expect German economy to grow</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:728c576a7f12a8834514cfddf9b77cfcef6da8f4e2ffac8155b3bf5b224f1582</id><updated>2026-09-24T20:03:42Z</updated><published>2026-09-24T17:04:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/after-several-difficult-years-economists-now-expect-german-economy-to-grow/a-79418591--9a99d252976e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/after-several-difficult-years-economists-now-expect-german-economy-to-grow/a-79418591?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Germany's economy is growing again, but recovery remains on shaky ground. High government spending is keeping the economy afloat, while energy prices, a shortage of skilled workers and debt continue to weigh on it.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Germany sets out plan to phase out fossil fuels by 2045</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:162ff625680a460ced0e888021bc9f6025fb0968ebf31f8089122e9867725a80</id><updated>2026-09-24T20:02:39Z</updated><published>2026-09-24T01:37:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-sets-out-plan-to-phase-out-fossil-fuels-by-2045/a-79404028--8330a10886c6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-sets-out-plan-to-phase-out-fossil-fuels-by-2045/a-79404028?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Germany has said it plans to phase out the use of coal, oil and gas by 2045, reaffirming a climate strategy focused on electrification.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Could a Left Party government in Berlin expropriate large real estate companies?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3859bdb84c548eef46d87d47d708aa41721841bd8365e8c773abe35e0752c4c6</id><updated>2026-09-24T20:02:39Z</updated><published>2026-09-23T14:49:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/could-a-left-party-government-in-berlin-expropriate-large-real-estate-companies/a-79399683--c9f46d7db0c4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/could-a-left-party-government-in-berlin-expropriate-large-real-estate-companies/a-79399683?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The socialist Left Party won the Berlin election partly on the promise to implement the city's 2021 expropriation referendum as a way to solve the city's rent crisis. But can it really happen?</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Germany's oldest party, the center-left SPD, is in a difficult position following its success in the Mecklenburg-Western Pomerania state election</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:71adb3412bc03d8bdcfb73f97bb32f22ff23891b4a1246cdd32a59ffa6c071f0</id><updated>2026-09-24T20:02:39Z</updated><published>2026-09-23T13:28:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-s-oldest-party-the-center-left-spd-is-in-a-difficult-position-following-its-success-in-the-m/a-79376827--2a4f42a68594.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-s-oldest-party-the-center-left-spd-is-in-a-difficult-position-following-its-success-in-the-mecklenburg-western-pomerania-state-election/a-79376827?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Chancellor Friedrich Merz (CDU) has vowed to press ahead with controversial reforms, but resistance is mounting within his coalition partner, the SPD. How much dissent can a governing coalition tolerate?</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Oktoberfest 2026: Everything you need to know</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3cbccf9af32cdf63c9de6475900a5f472f85406f291fd41048d07be45ce9b4c0</id><updated>2026-09-24T20:02:39Z</updated><published>2026-09-19T09:40:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/oktoberfest-2026-everything-you-need-to-know/a-79311285--1e3ee9d16248.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/oktoberfest-2026-everything-you-need-to-know/a-79311285?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">This year, AI will be used to manage overcrowded situations. Find all the numbers surrounding the fest — including the price of water!</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Saint, sinner or feminist icon: How Mary Magdalene's image evolved through time</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:10475d99568ef46e6b05f329349b3794a26cad58625799bdf37d419860531e14</id><updated>2026-09-24T20:02:39Z</updated><published>2026-09-17T07:06:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/saint-sinner-or-feminist-icon-how-mary-magdalene-s-image-evolved-through-time/a-79293868--1a6f3ade345e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/saint-sinner-or-feminist-icon-how-mary-magdalene-s-image-evolved-through-time/a-79293868?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">From "Apostle of the Apostles" to prostitute, Mary Magdalene has been assigned a wide variety of roles, as a new exhibition shows.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry></feed>
